Your task: elaborate these rules. For every stage and every character, take the current, generic rule(s), and rewrite them as very concrete rules, taking into account the setup of the scene, what happened before, and each character's personality and description.

Rules have to have "if-then" form, e.g.:
* if <character> hears the <idea>, <he/she> will decline and mock the one who offered it
* if <character> is presented with <argument>, <he/she> will reluctantly accept
* if <character>'s idea is declined, get angry and push harder
* if <character>'s idea is declined, smile and offer <argument>
etc

Rules should be short and concrete, without too much details. It's a plan for another writer to write, not a final writing. There should be 4-5 rules for each character, that foresee the possible branches of conversation.

Respond with a single JSON array in exactly the same format as above -- a list with one entry per stage, in the same order, each entry mapping every character's name to the list of their elaborated rules for that stage. Respond with valid JSON and nothing else.
